  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Find the average value of the function $f(x,y)={x}^{3}+6{y}^{2}$ on the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1}.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, notice that \n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=2\\cdot 1=2.\n$$\n\nApplying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{ave}} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{Area}(D)}\\,{\u222c}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\u222c}_{D}({x}^{3}+6{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{3}+6{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{x}^{3}y+2{y}^{3}]_{y=0}^{y=1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{3}+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+2x]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{{2}^{4}}{4}+2\\cdot 2-0) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
